== stdout
clai - (c)ommand (l)ine (a)rtificial (i)ntelligence

Prerequisites:
  - Set the environment variable to your API key according to the vendor you seek to use
  - (Optional) Set the NO_COLOR environment variable to disable ansi color output
  - (Optional) Install glow - https://github.com/charmbracelet/glow for formatted markdown output

Usage: clai [command flags] <command> [command flags] [args]

Commands:
  audio|a         Transcribe and record audio: audio t|transcribe <file> ('-' reads stdin), audio c|calibrate
  chat|c          Manage chats: continue|delete|list|dir|dirv2|summarize|help
  cloud           Your clai.chat account and sync (optional)
  completion      generate shell completion scripts (bash|zsh)
  config          The config store: edit, list, schema, validate, publish and dir
  dir-replay|dre  Replay the last message of the directory-scoped conversation
  help            Print this usage; 'clai help <command>' is that command's -h
  mcp             Manage MCP server state
  photo|p         Ask the photo model for a picture with the given prompt
  query|q         Query the chat model with the given text; -l iterates toward a goal
  replay|re       Replay the most recent message
  skills          Publish skills and use them from profiles
  tools|t         List available tools, or show details for a specific tool
  version         Print the version of clai and its dependencies
  video|v         Ask the video model for a video with the given prompt

Each command has its own flags, examples and subcommands in its help:
'clai help <command>' or 'clai <command> -h'. For example, 'clai query -h'
has the details of a query. A prompt that starts with '-' goes after '--':
'clai query -- -why does this fail'.

For scripts, -json before the command prints every line, on stdout and on
stderr, as one JSON record: 'clai -json query hi'.

Investigating:
  clai reports what it does on stderr, by subsystem. LOG_LEVEL sets how much
  is shown: first a level for everything (error, warn, info, debug or trace),
  then subsystem=level for the ones to look closer at. A name also selects
  the names under it, so vendor=debug is every vendor.

    LOG_LEVEL=debug clai query hi                     # everything
    LOG_LEVEL=warn,mcp=debug clai query hi            # MCP servers in detail
    LOG_LEVEL=warn,vendor=debug,call=debug clai ...   # requests and tool calls

  Each line names its subsystem in brackets, such as 'debug [config] ...',
  and with -json it is the record's "subsystem" field. So one run at debug
  shows which subsystem to narrow to.

Subsystems:
  clai                      the run itself: start, signals, shutdown
  config                    configuration files: loading and migrating
  setup                     the setup wizard and what it writes
  chat                      stored conversations: saving, listing, continuing
  dirscope                  which conversation belongs to the directory
  reply_mode                replay and reply: the conversation being continued
  profiles                  profiles: loading, validating, installing
  skills                    skills: discovery, trust and loading
  cloud                     the clai.chat account and its sync
  text_querier              a query: prompt setup, steps, retries, fallback
  call                      each tool call and its result
  summary                   conversation titles and summaries
  lookback                  recent conversations surfaced to the model
  stoploss                  the token and tool-call limits of a run
  cost_manager              token prices and the cost of a run
  openrouter_model_catalog  OpenRouter's model and price list
  tools                     which built-in tools a run is given
  tools_registry_set        each tool as it is registered
  mcp                       MCP servers: start, handshake, schema cache
  glob                      the files a -glob pattern adds to the prompt
  audio                     recording and transcription
  photo                     image generation
  video                     video generation
  verbose                   extra detail: saved chat paths, raw stream tokens
  claudified_msgs           the messages as sent to Anthropic
  vendor.openai             requests to and responses from OpenAI
  vendor.anthropic          requests to and responses from Anthropic
  vendor.openrouter         requests to and responses from OpenRouter
  vendor.mistral            requests to and responses from Mistral
  vendor.huggingface        requests to and responses from Hugging Face
  vendor.berget             requests to and responses from Berget
  vendor.deepseek           requests to and responses from DeepSeek
  vendor.gemini             requests to and responses from Gemini
  vendor.inception          requests to and responses from Inception
  vendor.novita             requests to and responses from Novita
  vendor.ollama             requests to and responses from Ollama
  vendor.xai                requests to and responses from xAI

Config dir: $CONFIG
Cache dir:  $CONFIG/cache

